    <description>Users shouldn&apos;t be allowed to create a duplicate contact if the Last name and the Email address match. We should have the user provide the error message &quot; There is a duplicate existing contact; please update an existing contact; this should apply to the Contact data load for the CDM team.

Gitlab #31919
1. When the user tries to create a new contact record, where in the system the existing name and email address** in the contact record do exist, then an Error message should be displayed: You are unable to create this record as this contact already exists in Salesforce, please search for the contact and associate it to the relevant account records.
2. Exclude PSA contact record type    
3. Excluded for the EDP Integration user, Sierra26 integration users, and exclude Account Payable and the email address indiainvoices@ironmountain.com.</description>
